/*!
    \page add-update-remove-components.html

    \title Add, update, and remove installed Qt components
    \brief Add, update, or remove installed Qt components with \QMT.

    \QMT is included in every Qt installation. Use it to add, update, and remove installed
    components. The tool is located in your Qt installation directory (typically \c{C:/Qt/}).

    \image {maintenancetool.webp} {Add, remove, and update components in \QMT}


    You can also use \QMT with the command-line interface, which is useful if you are:
    \list
      \li Updating installations on multiple machines.
      \li Working with CI/CD pipelines.
      \li Automating updates without user interaction.
    \endlist


    For more information about using \QMT with the command-line,
    see \l{Get and Install Qt with Command Line Interface}.

*/
